---

<section id="best-practices" class="py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">
    YAML Best Practices
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Follow these guidelines to write clean, maintainable, and error-free YAML files.</p>
  <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
    {[
      { title: 'Use consistent indentation', desc: 'Pick 2 or 4 spaces and stick with it throughout your entire file. Most teams standardize on 2 spaces for YAML. Configure your editor to insert spaces when you press Tab. Never mix indentation styles in the same file.' },
      { title: 'Quote strings that could be ambiguous', desc: 'Values like yes, no, true, false, null, and strings containing special characters (: { } [ ] , & * ? | - < > = ! % @ `) should always be quoted. Use single quotes for literal strings and double quotes when you need escape sequences.' },
      { title: 'Add meaningful comments', desc: 'YAML supports comments with the # character. Document the purpose of complex blocks, note required fields, and explain non-obvious values. Comments are preserved by our formatter during formatting.' },
      { title: 'Use anchors and aliases for repeated blocks', desc: 'YAML anchors (&name) and aliases (*name) let you define a block once and reuse it multiple times. This reduces duplication and makes updates easier. Our formatter fully preserves anchor/alias relationships.' },
      { title: 'Separate configuration from secrets', desc: 'Never store API keys, passwords, or tokens directly in YAML files committed to version control. Use environment variables, secret management tools, or Kubernetes secrets instead.' },
      { title: 'Validate and format before committing', desc: 'Always run your YAML through a formatter and validator before pushing to your repository. Our tool catches syntax errors, normalizes indentation, and ensures your YAML is production-ready in seconds.' },
      { title: 'Use multi-document files for related resources', desc: 'YAML supports multiple documents in a single file using the --- separator. Group related Kubernetes resources or CI/CD job definitions together for better organization, and our formatter handles each document independently.' },
      { title: 'Prefer flow style for simple inline mappings', desc: 'For short key-value pairs that fit on one line, YAML flow style ({key: value}) is more readable than block style. Reserve block style for nested structures and longer values.' },
    ].map(({title, desc}) => (
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-6 h-6 mt-0.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/30 flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">{title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">{desc}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
